[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human muscle (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,321): skew = -0.248, excess kurtosis = -0.195, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.06e-24, Jarque-Bera p = 1.36e-24
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.485, excess kurtosis = 0.475, D'Agostino K^2 p = 3.97e-85, Jarque-Bera p = 3.52e-99
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 278.138, p = 1.77e-29
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 4.426, p = 0.012
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/muscle/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_muscle.png
